issues:
The UI flow test fails at the Export step because clicking the **Export** button on the Settings screen does not navigate to the Export screen. The `goTo` function in `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx` only tries to navigate using `navigation.getParent()?.navigate(screen)`. In the current navigation hierarchy this can return `undefined`, so the navigation never occurs and the Export screen (and its Export CSV/PDF buttons) are never shown, causing the "Export ready to share" expectation to time out.

**Fix:** Update the `goTo` helper to attempt navigation on the parent navigator if it exists, otherwise fall back to navigating on the current navigator. For example:
```tsx
const goTo = (screen: string) => {
  const parent = navigation.getParent?.();
  if (parent) {
    // Navigate on the parent stack (Export, AppLock, TaxSettings are defined there)
    parent.navigate(screen as never);
  } else {
    // Fallback: navigate on the current navigator (covers cases where the screen is in the same navigator)
    navigation.navigate(screen as never);
  }
};
```
This change ensures the Export button correctly opens the Export screen, and similarly fixes navigation for AppLock and Tax Settings screens.

Optionally, remove the unused `getStore` import from this file to keep linting clean.
